.TH GIRL 1 2026-10-09 girlpages "girlpages Manual"
.SH NAME
girl \- an interface to the system reference manuals, but make it girly
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B girl
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ section ]
.IR page \ ...
.br
.B girl
.B \-k
.IR regexp \ ...
.br
.B girl
.B \-f
.IR page \ ...
.br
.B girl
.B \-r
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ section ]
.IR page \ ...
.br
.B girl
.B \-\-bulk
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ section \ ...]
.br
.B girl
.B \-\-serve
.RB [ \-\-listen =\fIaddress\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B girl
works like
.BR man (1):
it finds the manual page you ask for and shows it in a pager.
The difference is that the page is first rewritten by a large language model
in the voice of a Gen Z teenage girl, with colour and emoji, while keeping
every option, argument, default, file, example and caveat of the original.
.PP
Pages are found with
.BR "man \-w" ,
so names, sections and search order behave exactly as they do for
.BR man .
.PP
.B girl rfc
.I number
(or
.BI rfc number\fR)
shows an RFC from the repository (see
.BR REPOSITORIES ):
girlified if it's been, the original otherwise.
The page is rendered to plain text with
.BR man ,
sent to the model, and the result is stored in a cache.
If a page is already cached it is shown straight away without contacting the
model; this includes pages whose source has since changed, which are shown
with a note until they are refreshed.
.PP
Identical pages (such as aliases made with symbolic links or
.B .so
requests) share one conversion.
Long pages are split at section boundaries and converted in parts.
If the model leaves out any command-line options that appear in the original,
the part is retried once with a list of what went missing.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS "Options shared with man"
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-all
Show every matching page, not just the first.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-S ", " \-\-sections =\fIlist\fR
Only search the given sections, separated by colons or commas.
A section can also be given as the first argument, as in
.BR "girl 3 printf" .
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-apropos
Search page names and descriptions.
This runs
.B man \-k
directly.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-whatis
Show one-line descriptions.
This runs
.B man \-f
directly.
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-where ", " \-\-path ", " \-\-location
Print the location of the source pages instead of showing them.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-local\-file
Treat each argument as a man page file rather than a page name.
.TP
.BR \-M ", " \-\-manpath =\fIpath\fR
Search
.I path
instead of the default manual path.
.TP
.BR \-L ", " \-\-locale =\fIlocale\fR
Look for pages in this locale.
.TP
.BR \-P ", " \-\-pager =\fIpager\fR
Use
.I pager
to display output.
.TP
.BR \-C ", " \-\-config\-file =\fIfile\fR
Read
.I file
instead of the user configuration file.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a summary of options.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version.
.SS "Display options"
.TP
.B \-\-refresh
Convert the page again even if it is cached, replacing the cached copy.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-cache
Always convert the page with the model, without looking in the cache or the
repository, and save nothing: the cache stays as it was. Only for reading
pages, not with
.BR \-\-cached\-only ,
.BR \-\-bulk ,
.BR \-\-serve
and the like.
.TP
.B \-\-cached\-only
Never contact the model; fail for pages that are neither cached nor in the
repository (see
.BR REPOSITORIES ).
.TP
.B \-\-raw
Print the stored markup instead of rendering it.
.TP
.B \-\-html
Write the page as a self-contained HTML document on standard output, with
the stylesheet inlined, instead of showing it in the pager.
Several pages go into one document.
.TP
.BR \-\-color =\fIwhen\fR
Use colour
.BR always ,
.BR never ,
or
.B auto
(the default), which uses colour when standard output is a terminal and
.B NO_COLOR
is not set.
.TP
.BR \-\-provider =\fIname\fR
Use the provider configured as
.BI [providers. name ]
(see
.BR CONFIGURATION ),
overriding
.BR provider .
.B \-\-backend
and
.B \-\-model
still apply on top of it.
.TP
.BR \-\-backend =\fIname\fR
Use the
.BR auto ,
.BR openai ,
or
.B claude
backend, overriding the configuration.
.TP
.BR \-\-model =\fImodel\fR
Ask this model, overriding the configuration.
.TP
.BR \-\-repo =\fIurl\fR
Fetch pages from this girlpages repository before asking the model,
overriding the configuration;
.B none
switches the configured one off.
.TP
.B \-\-doctor
Show which configuration files were read, which backend and model will be
used, and what each cache holds.
.SS "Web options"
.TP
.B \-\-serve
Run a web server for browsing pages by section, searching their names and
descriptions, and reading them.
Pages that are not cached are converted when someone opens them; see
.BR "WEB SERVER" .
.TP
.BR \-\-listen =\fIaddress\fR
Where
.B \-\-serve
listens, as
.IR host : port .
The default is
.BR localhost:1989 .
.SS "Repository options"
.TP
.BR \-\-import =\fIsource\fR
Fill the cache with every installed page the girlpages repository
.I source
(a URL or a directory: the repository, or a site with it in
.BR repo/ )
has, without asking a model.
Pages it doesn't have are counted, not treated as failures, and an import
doesn't count as a full
.B \-\-bulk
run.
Sections can be given as for
.BR \-\-bulk ,
or page names to import just those, along with
.BR \-j ", " \-\-limit ", " \-\-force
(fetch again, replacing what's cached), \-n
and
.BR \-q .
The pages are used even if
.B extra_instructions
is set, since you asked for them.
.TP
.BR \-\-export =\fIdir\fR
Write every cached page that's up to date with the installed page into a
girlpages repository in
.IR dir /repo
(adding to one already there), with the installed package each came from,
and publish it, ready for
.BR "girl \-\-import" ,
.BR "girlrepo import" ,
or serving as it is;
.B girlrepo \-d
.I dir
.B publish
adds a website.
.B \-s
limits it to some sections, and
.B \-n
says what would be exported.
.SS "Remote options"
These read pages straight from the repository (see
.BR REPOSITORIES ),
whether or not they're installed here, in any version and variant it has.
Nothing is cached, and no model is asked.
.BR girlc (1)
does the same on its own, for machines without
.BR girl .
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-remote
Read pages from the repository instead of this system.
Pages are named as for
.BR man :
.RI [ section ]
.IR page ,
or
.IR page ( section ),
and a page named alone is the first by
.BR man 's
section order (in any case, as
.B man
finds them).
.BR \-a ", " \-s " and " \-P
work as they do for local pages, and
.BR \-k " and " \-f
search the repository rather than the system's
.B whatis
database:
.B \-k
searches for each argument, by the words in pages' names, descriptions and
text (a quoted argument of several words finds pages with all of them first).
If the latest version isn't girlified yet, its original is shown, saying
which version is, if any.
.TP
.BR \-\-page\-version =\fIversion\fR
Which version of a page to read: its version number
.RB ( 9.7 ),
where it's from
.RB ( debian ", " debian/trixie
or
.BR "debian trixie" ,
for the latest from there), or the start of its source hash.
The default is the latest.
.TP
.BR \-\-variant =\fIname\fR
Which variant to read:
.B girl
(the default),
.B man
(the original) or any other the repository has.
.TP
.B \-\-versions
List a page's versions, with how to pick each, where it's from, and its
variants, instead of reading it.
.TP
.B \-\-ngrams
With
.BR \-k ,
also find words inside other words
.RB ( dir
finds
.B mkdir
and
.BR readdir ),
as the website's \(lqparts of words\(rq search does.
.PP
.BR \-\-page\-version ", " \-\-variant " and " \-\-versions
imply
.BR \-r .
.SS "Bulk options"
.TP
.BR \-\-batch =\fIapi\fR
Send pages in batches with
.BR openrouter ,
.BR anthropic ,
.BR sail ,
or
.B none
(see
.BR batches ),
overriding the configuration.
.TP
.B \-\-reprompt
Convert again pages made with an older prompt (the prompt's version is
recorded with every conversion; see
.BR \-\-doctor ),
not taking such conversions from the cache or a repository.
Ordinary runs, and the hooks, leave them be: a new prompt shouldn't cost a
whole system's worth of conversions unless you ask.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-batch
The same as
.BR \-\-batch=none .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-wait
Send batches off and return without waiting for them; the next
.B \-\-bulk
run collects them.
.TP
.B \-\-bulk
Convert every page in the manual path (the top-level
.BI man N
directories; translations are skipped), most useful sections first.
Pages that are already cached and unchanged are skipped, so running it again
only does new work.
Sections may be given as arguments, as in
.BR "girl \-\-bulk 1 8" .
After a complete run without section or limit filters,
.B \-\-update
runs also convert new pages.
.TP
.B \-\-update
Refresh pages whose source has changed since they were converted.
If a complete
.B \-\-bulk
run has been done in this cache before, new pages are converted too;
otherwise only pages that are already cached are looked at.
This is what the package-manager hooks and timers run.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Convert pages even if they are up to date.
.TP
.B \-\-prune
After a complete run, remove cache entries for pages that no longer exist and
conversions that nothing refers to.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
List the pages that would be converted, and convert nothing.
No backend is needed.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-jobs =\fIn\fR
Send up to
.I n
requests to the model at once.
.TP
.BR \-\-limit =\fIn\fR
Only look at the first
.I n
pages.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Only report errors.
.SH BACKENDS
.SS claude
Runs the
.BR claude (1)
command-line tool in print mode:
.PP
.RS
.nf
claude \-p \-\-output\-format text \-\-no\-session\-persistence \e
    \-\-system\-prompt \fIprompt\fR \-\-tools "" \-\-strict\-mcp\-config \e
    \-\-disable\-slash\-commands \-\-setting\-sources "" [\-\-model \fImodel\fR]
.fi
.RE
.PP
with the page on standard input, from the temporary directory, so that the
user's own MCP servers, skills, hooks and project files stay out of it.
.SS openai
Posts to the
.B /chat/completions
endpoint of any OpenAI-compatible API, such as OpenAI, OpenRouter, Ollama,
llama.cpp, vLLM or LM Studio.
Rate-limited and failed requests are retried.
.SS auto
The default.
Uses
.B openai
if
.B openai.base_url
is set to something other than OpenAI's own endpoint, otherwise
.B claude
if the command is on
.BR PATH ,
otherwise
.B openai
if an API key is configured.
.SS "completion windows"
Some servers (Sail's, at
.BR https://api.sailresearch.com/v1 )
let requests wait for a lower price.
.B openai.completion_window
picks how long:
.B asap
(straight away),
.B balanced
(queued for a while) or
.B flex
(cheapest, whenever there's room).
With
.B openai.api
set to
.BR responses ,
girl uses the Responses API, and sends requests that wait in the background,
checking on each until it's done (a request retried after a failure is sent
with the same idempotency key, so it isn't run twice);
.B flex
works only that way.
Chat completions (the default) can be
.B asap
or
.BR balanced ,
waiting for the reply.
.SS "batches"
.B \-\-bulk
can send every page that needs converting in batches rather than one request
at a time: about half the price, and back within a day.
.B batch
picks the API:
.B openrouter
uses OpenRouter's batch endpoint
.RB ( openai.batch_url ,
which defaults to
.BR https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/batches ;
setting it turns this on) with the
.B [openai]
key and model;
.B anthropic
uses Anthropic's Message Batches API with the
.B [anthropic]
settings, which need an Anthropic API key (the claude CLI's login isn't used);
.B sail
uses Sail's batch API
.RB ( openai.base_url
plus
.BR /batches ,
or
.BR openai.batch_url ),
which always runs in Sail's cheapest completion window,
.BR flex ,
with the
.B [openai]
key and model;
.B none
turns batches off.
Big runs are split to stay under each API's size limit.
.PP
Batches are saved in the cache's
.B batches
directory as they're sent.
Unless
.B \-\-no\-wait
is given, the run waits, checking every
.B openai.batch_poll
.RB ( 1m );
interrupting it is safe, as every
.B \-\-bulk
run starts by collecting whatever has finished and doesn't send pages that are
still out.
Ctrl+C asks a run to stop; a second stops it right away.
Batches sent with one API are only collected while that API is configured.
A page that changed in the meantime is sent again.
Replies get the same completeness check as live ones, and any part that failed
or dropped options is redone live, if the backend works; batches don't need
it otherwise.
The package-manager hooks and timer pass
.BR \-\-no\-wait ,
so the daily run collects what the last one sent.
.SH "WEB SERVER"
.B girl \-\-serve
lists every page in the manual path by section, with descriptions from the
.BR whatis
database and a ✨ marker on pages already converted.
The search box matches page names and descriptions;
searching for a reference such as
.B printf(3)
goes straight to that page.
References to other pages and URLs inside a page become links, and each page
has a table of contents and a link to the unconverted original.
.PP
Opening a page that is not cached starts converting it and shows a waiting
page that refreshes itself until it is done.
Visitors asking for the same page share one conversion, and no more than
.B jobs
requests are sent to the model at once across all of them.
A page can also be converted again from its
.B re-girlify
button.
With
.BR \-\-cached\-only ,
or when no backend is configured, only cached pages are shown.
.PP
The pages follow the browser's light or dark preference
(pink and white in the light, purple and black in the dark), and a button
switches between them.
.PP
There is no authentication.
Anyone who can reach the server can make it send pages to the model,
so keep it on
.B localhost
or use
.B \-\-cached\-only
when listening anywhere else.
.SH REPOSITORIES
A girlpages repository is a set of pages someone else has already girlified,
published as static files by
.BR girlrepo (1).
The official one is girlpages.dev's,
.BR https://girlpages.dev/repo ,
which
.B girl
uses unless
.B [repo] url
says another (or
.BR none ).
A page that isn't cached is looked for there before the model is asked, and
cached like any other.
Pages are found by the SHA-256 of their roff source (decompressed, with
.B .so
requests followed), so only a conversion of exactly the version installed
here is used; anything else is converted as usual.
Pages are fetched one at a time as they are read (and by
.BR \-\-bulk ),
so the repository learns which pages are read, but nothing else.
.PP
The repository isn't used with
.BR \-\-refresh ,
or when
.B extra_instructions
is set, since those ask for a page made just for you.
.B \-\-bulk
works without a model when there's a repository, caching what the
repository has.
To use no repository at all (so nothing is asked of any but the model),
set
.B url = \(dqnone\(dq
in
.BR [repo] ,
or
.BR GIRLPAGES_REPO=none .
.PP
.B girl \-r
reads any page in the repository, installed here or not, in any version
and variant (see
.BR "Remote options" );
so does
.BR girlc (1).
.SH CONFIGURATION
Settings are read from the system configuration file, then the user
configuration file (or the file given with
.BR \-C ),
then the environment, with later sources winning.
The files are in TOML:
.PP
.RS
.nf
backend = "auto"         # auto, openai or claude
jobs = 4                 # requests at once
chunk_size = 12000       # bytes of text per request
cache_dir = ""           # where to write conversions
pager = ""
batch = ""               # openrouter, anthropic, sail or none, for \-\-bulk
batch_max_requests = 0   # requests per batch, at most (0: the API's limit)
extra_instructions = ""  # appended to the prompt

[claude]
command = "claude"
model = "haiku"
args = []
timeout = "15m"

[openai]
base_url = "https://api.openai.com/v1"
model = ""
api_key = ""
api_key_file = ""
temperature = 0.9
max_tokens = 16000
timeout = "10m"
api = "chat"             # chat (completions) or responses
completion_window = ""   # asap, balanced or flex (Sail); flex needs responses
batch_url = ""           # an OpenRouter batch endpoint, for \-\-bulk
batch_poll = "1m"

[openai.headers]
"X\-Example" = "value"

[openai.extra]           # added to each request's body, e.g. OpenRouter's
provider = { only = ["deepinfra"], allow_fallbacks = false }
reasoning = { enabled = false }

[anthropic]
api_key = ""             # or ANTHROPIC_API_KEY; for batch = "anthropic"
api_key_file = ""
model = "claude\-haiku\-5\-5"
max_tokens = 32000
batch_url = "https://api.anthropic.com/v1/messages/batches"
timeout = "10m"

[repo]
url = "https://girlpages.dev/repo"   # a girlpages repository, or "none"
timeout = "20s"
.fi
.RE
.SS Providers
Rather than editing
.B [openai]
or
.B [claude]
to switch between services, name each one in a
.BI [providers. name ]
section and pick one with
.BR provider ,
.B GIRLPAGES_PROVIDER
or
.BR \-\-provider :
.PP
.RS
.nf
provider = "sail"        # the default, if any

[providers.sail]
base_url = "https://api.sailresearch.com/v1"
model = "deepseek\-ai/DeepSeek\-V4.1\-Flash"
api_key_file = "/home/me/.config/girlpages/sail\-key"
api = "responses"
completion_window = "flex"
max_tokens = 32000
batch = "sail"           # its own batch API, if any
batch_max_requests = 3000

[providers.openrouter]
base_url = "https://openrouter.ai/api/v1"
model = "anthropic/claude\-haiku\-5.5"
api_key_file = "/home/me/.config/girlpages/openrouter\-key"

[providers.haiku]
backend = "claude"       # the claude CLI; the default is openai
model = "claude\-haiku\-5\-5"
batch = "anthropic"      # Message Batches, with [anthropic]
api_key_file = "/home/me/.config/girlpages/anthropic\-key"
.fi
.RE
.PP
A provider takes any of
.BR [openai] 's
settings (with
.BR "backend = \(dqclaude\(dq" ,
any of
.BR [claude] 's),
and its own
.B batch
and
.BR batch_max_requests :
the top\-level ones don't apply to it, and a provider with no
.B batch
doesn't batch.
.B batch = \(dqanthropic\(dq
uses
.BR [anthropic] ,
with the provider's
.B api_key
or
.B api_key_file
if it has one.
It stands alone: whatever it doesn't set is the default, not what
.B [openai]
or another provider says, so one service's key or headers are never sent to
another.
For the same reason,
.BR OPENAI_API_KEY ,
.B OPENAI_BASE_URL
and the other connection settings in the environment are ignored when a
provider is in use; the rest still apply.
With no provider chosen,
.B [openai]
and
.B [claude]
are used, as ever.
.PP
A system configuration file that holds an API key should not be world-readable;
use
.B api_key_file
pointing at a file only root can read, and users will still see every page the
system cache already has.
.SH CACHE
Conversions are stored as
.BI objects/ xx / sha256 .girl
files named by the hash of the plain-text page, with an index under
.B index/
that maps each source file to its conversion and records the source's size and
modification time.
.PP
.B girl
reads the cache it writes to and the system cache.
It writes to
.B cache_dir
if that is set, to the system cache when run as root, and to the user's cache
otherwise.
When the same page is in both, an up-to-date copy is preferred.
.SH "PACKAGE MANAGER HOOKS"
A system-wide install adds a hook for each package manager it finds:
an apt
.B DPkg::Post\-Invoke
hook, a pacman hook on
.BR usr/share/man/* ,
and a dnf post-transaction action.
Each runs
.BR girlpages\-hook ,
which starts
.B girlpages\-update.service
(or, without systemd, a background
.BR "girl \-\-bulk \-\-update \-\-prune" )
and never fails the transaction.
A daily
.B girlpages\-update.timer
catches pages installed any other way.
A per-user install gets the same timer as a user unit.
.PP
Since
.B \-\-update
only converts new pages after a complete
.B \-\-bulk
run, the hooks cost nothing until an administrator opts in with
.BR "sudo girl \-\-bulk" .
.PP
The service runs as root.
When using the
.B claude
backend, root's
.B claude
must be logged in, or point
.B claude.command
at a wrapper.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GIRLPAGER
Pager to use; checked before
.BR PAGER .
.B MANPAGER
is not used, as it often removes formatting.
.TP
.B PAGER
Pager to use if
.B GIRLPAGER
is not set.
The default is
.BR less ,
which is given
.B \-R
so colours come through.
.TP
.B MANWIDTH
Width to lay pages out at.
Otherwise the terminal width is used, up to 100 columns.
.TP
.B MANPATH
As for
.BR man .
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Turns colour off.
.TP
.B GIRLPAGES_CONFIG
User configuration file to read.
.TP
.B GIRLPAGES_PROVIDER
Overrides
.BR provider .
.TP
.BR GIRLPAGES_BACKEND ", " GIRLPAGES_MODEL ", " GIRLPAGES_JOBS ", " GIRLPAGES_CACHE_DIR
Override
.BR backend ,
the model,
.B jobs
and
.BR cache_dir .
.TP
.BR GIRLPAGES_OPENAI_BASE_URL ", " OPENAI_BASE_URL
Override
.BR openai.base_url .
.TP
.BR GIRLPAGES_OPENAI_API_KEY ", " OPENAI_API_KEY
Override
.BR openai.api_key .
.TP
.BR GIRLPAGES_OPENAI_MODEL ", " GIRLPAGES_CLAUDE_MODEL ", " GIRLPAGES_CLAUDE_COMMAND
Override the per-backend settings.
.TP
.B GIRLPAGES_REPO
Overrides
.BR repo.url .
.TP
.B GIRLPAGES_OPENAI_BATCH_URL
Overrides
.BR openai.batch_url .
.TP
.B GIRLPAGES_BATCH
Overrides
.BR batch .
.TP
.BR GIRLPAGES_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY ", " ANTHROPIC_API_KEY ", " GIRLPAGES_ANTHROPIC_MODEL
Override
.B anthropic.api_key
and
.BR anthropic.model .
.TP
.BR XDG_CONFIG_HOME ", " XDG_CACHE_HOME
Locate the user configuration file and cache.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/girlpages/config.toml
System configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.config/girlpages/config.toml
User configuration.
.TP
.I /var/cache/girlpages
System cache.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/girlpages
User cache.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Usage or configuration error.
.TP
.B 2
A page could not be converted, or a bulk run had failures.
.TP
.B 16
A page was not found.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B girl ls
Show
.BR ls (1).
.TP
.B girl 3 printf
Show
.BR printf (3)
rather than
.BR printf (1).
.TP
.B girl \-\-refresh \-\-model opus tar
Convert
.BR tar (1)
again with a different model.
.TP
.B sudo girl \-\-bulk \-j 8 1 8
Convert every page in sections 1 and 8 into the system cache, eight at a time.
.TP
.B girl \-\-bulk \-\-dry\-run
See how many pages a full run would convert.
.TP
.B girl \-\-html ls > ls.html
Save
.BR ls (1)
as a web page.
.TP
.B girl \-\-serve
Browse the manual at
.BR http://localhost:1989/ .
.TP
.B girl \-\-export ~/girlpages && girl \-\-import ~/girlpages
Share conversions between machines: export on one, import on the others
(the directory can be anywhere they can read, or a web server).
.TP
.B girl \-r open
Read
.BR open (1)
from the repository, though it isn't installed.
.TP
.B girl \-r \-\-versions ls
.PD 0
.TP
.B girl \-r \-\-page\-version debian/bookworm \-\-variant man ls
.PD
See which versions of
.BR ls (1)
the repository has, then read the original of Debian bookworm's.
.TP
.B girl \-r \-k \-\-ngrams dir
Search the repository for pages about anything with
.B dir
in it.
.TP
.B girl \-\-repo https://mirror.example/repo \-\-bulk
Fill the cache with every page the repository has girlified, converting the
rest.
.SH BUGS
The model can still get things wrong.
When something matters, check the original with
.BR man .
.PP
Report bugs at
.UR https://github.com/NaomiAmethyst/girlpages/issues
.UE .
